{% extends 'base.tmpl' %}

{% block pre %}
<b>Scheduled maintenance: Nectar Database service upgrade</b>
<br/>
<br/>
We are upgrading the Nectar Database service (OpenStack Trove) to a new
release. This maintenance requires an outage of the Database service API and
a short outage of every database instance, including the instance listed
below.
{% endblock %}

{% block release_notes %}
{% endblock %}

{% block upgrade %}
{% if database.hostname %}
Hostname: <b>{{ database.hostname }}</b>
<br/>
{% endif %}
{% if database.ip %}
Current IP address: <b>{{ database.ip | join(', ') }}</b>
<br/>
{% endif %}
<br/>
<b>When</b>
<br/>
The maintenance window starts at <b>{{ start }}</b> and ends at
<b>{{ end }}</b>.
<br/>
<br/>
<b>What will happen</b>
<ul>
  <li>
    <b>Database service API outage (about 1 day):</b> for the whole
    maintenance window you will not be able to create, modify, resize, back
    up or delete database instances through the Nectar Research Cloud
    dashboard or the OpenStack CLI. Running instances will keep serving
    connections until we migrate them.
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Database instance outage (about 1 hour):</b> as part of the upgrade we
    will back up each database instance and recreate it from that
    <a href="https://tutorials.rc.nectar.org.au/database/04-database-backups">backup</a>.
    Your instance will be unavailable while this happens. For most instances
    the outage will be about 1 hour, depending on how long the backup takes.
    Larger databases will be unavailable for longer.
  </li>
</ul>
{% if used != "Unknown" %}
<b>Your instance is currently using {{ used }}GB.</b>
<br/>
<br/>
{% endif %}
<b>New IP address, same hostname</b>
<br/>
Your recreated database instance will have a <b>new IP address</b>. We will
update the existing DNS hostname for your instance to point to the new
address, so connections that use the hostname will keep working without any
change on your side.
<br/>
<br/>
If any of your applications or scripts connect using the IP address instead
of the hostname, please change them to use the hostname before the maintenance
window. Connections to the old IP address will stop working once your
instance has been recreated.
<br/>
<br/>
<b>What you need to do</b>
<br/>
You do not need to do anything for the upgrade itself. We will back up and
recreate your instance for you and restore your data from the
<a href="https://tutorials.rc.nectar.org.au/database/04-database-backups">backup</a>.
Before the maintenance window, we ask that you:
<ul>
  <li>
    Check that your applications connect using the hostname
    {% if database.hostname %}<b>{{ database.hostname }}</b>{% endif %}
    rather than the IP address, and update them if needed.
  </li>
  <li>
    Check that your applications reconnect automatically after a database
    outage, or plan to restart them after the maintenance window.
  </li>
  <li>
    <a href="https://tutorials.rc.nectar.org.au/database/04-database-backups">Create
    your own backup</a> of your database instance as a precaution. You can
    find more information in the Nectar Database service support
    documentation at
    https://support.ehelp.edu.au/support/solutions/articles/6000178670
  </li>
  <li>
    Avoid scheduling jobs that depend on your database during the
    maintenance window.
  </li>
</ul>
We apologise for any inconvenience this maintenance may cause.
<br/>
<br/>
{% endblock %}
